			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4650401">
									

<p>There's no reason this anomaly is Uncle Sam narrative-wise besides just being a hook which fails to follow through. Besides that, the meat of this article is the characterization of the anomaly<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-965975-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-965975-1')">1</a></sup>, which fails to capture me due to a lack of tension and conflict. Sure, he disagrees with the ASCI over whether he should be contained, but it's never developed beyond &quot;I'm a patriot and all, but goddamn guys I'm not going to keep turning children into Spam.&quot; The Foundation is secretly using his ability to essentially feed human meat to D-Class, but he never gets a chance to respond to it and grow as a character. This article is thwacked off at the trunk, so the anomaly never gets the chance to grow into a truly fleshed-out character.</p>
<p>This is a -1 from me.</p>
